<title>BELGIUM: Single market legislation table.</title>
<headline>Single market legislation table.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Here is a table of Commission statistics showing state of implementation of the measures in the 1985 white paper on creating the single market.</p>
<p>First figure shows number of single market measures notified/implemented by each member state, plus measures which are not applicable to that member states and possible derogations. Second figure is percentage of first figure in relation to total of 217 single market measures requiring national implementing measures.</p>
<p> The Netherlands     215     99.1 percent</p>
<p> Denmark		 215     99.1</p>
<p> Finland		 212     97.7</p>
<p> Luxembourg	    211     97.2</p>
<p> Britain		 210     96.8</p>
<p> Sweden		  208     95.9</p>
<p> Ireland		 208     95.9</p>
<p> Greece		  206     94.9</p>
<p> Portugal		205     94.5</p>
<p> France		  205     94.5</p>
<p> Belgium		 204     94.0</p>
<p> Spain		   202     93.1</p>
<p> Italy		   201     92.6</p>
<p> Austria		 192     88.5</p>
<p> Germany		 191     88.0</p>
</text>
